<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/195bc085-97d3-4f98-a026-c8670dad8945> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/195bc085-97d3-4f98-a026-c8670dad8945> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "pluralize gives -o and -f/-fe nouns a plain -s unless WordNet's form list has an -oes or -ves form (83 of 628 -o lemmas, 38 of 269 -f/-fe lemmas): potatoes, heroes, wolves and knives come from the data; photos, roofs and chiefs get -s.\n- LEMMA_TO_PLURAL holds every WordNet noun form, unfiltered.\n- Class D (generator refuses until classified) covers two cases: (a) a lemma with 2+ forms, which includes self-forms such as gas {gas, gasses} and genus {genera, genus}; (b) a lemma whose only form is the regular plural with the final consonant doubled (bus→busses, quiz→quizzes, fez→fezzes).\n- These are resolved in PLURAL_CHOICE. Its value must be a WordNet form of the lemma or regular_plural(lemma): bus→buses, gas→gases, quiz→quizzes.\n- A lemma whose single form equals itself (forceps, apparatus) pluralizes unchanged.\n- Precedence: overrides, then invariant, then irregular (supplement, PLURAL_CHOICE, WordNet), then regular rules." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/195bc085-97d3-4f98-a026-c8670dad8945> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/195bc085-97d3-4f98-a026-c8670dad8945> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/195bc085-97d3-4f98-a026-c8670dad8945> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:57:41.305336Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
