<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/41f2fbe8-7472-46c1-a5ef-bd1249002e24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/b9851667-ab87-40ac-bffd-99cd5802ffd2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/41f2fbe8-7472-46c1-a5ef-bd1249002e24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/41f2fbe8-7472-46c1-a5ef-bd1249002e24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "pluralize returns the word unchanged when the singularize core would change it: a plural-form noun (glasses, arms, metrics), an irregular plural (men, people, mice), or a fallback-recognised plural (widgets, IDs). It also leaves unchanged an unknown word ending in a plural-looking -s, including capitalised ones (Kubernetes, Postgres). This keeps pluralize from ever producing glasseses or Kuberneteses. It refines step 2 of D7." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/41f2fbe8-7472-46c1-a5ef-bd1249002e24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/41f2fbe8-7472-46c1-a5ef-bd1249002e24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T19:10:48.093176Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
