<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5f94288a-36c5-4b9d-a024-dde8dd385cd9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Add `singularize_phrase` and `pluralize_phrase` as free functions and as Inflector methods, returning Cow<'_, str>. They find the last maximal run of non-whitespace characters, inflect it with the matching word function (same overrides, case handling and guess_unknown setting), and keep the text before and after it byte-for-byte (\"order lines\"→\"order line\", \"Order Lines\"→\"Order Line\", \"dry dock\"→\"dry docks\"). Input with no whitespace behaves exactly like the word function; empty or all-whitespace input is unchanged. Borrowed iff unchanged. The README and the word functions' docs state that whitespace input is returned unchanged and point to the phrase functions; is_noun's docs state it returns false for whitespace input; the guess_unknown docs state that capitalised words are never guessed (P3). Fixes GitHub issue #2. New public API, so the release is 0.2.0." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5f94288a-36c5-4b9d-a024-dde8dd385cd9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
