<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b442d17-b6d3-49ea-955b-6600cb36c4c6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/e8c93060-59ea-404d-b1a0-61eeb41946e8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "P6: -man/-men and -sis/-ses rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/5716d820-8bd9-4f9e-90b0-257b9c4a72f2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/cdaaaded-bd10-485e-a590-f298e66ab80d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "WordNet lists -men forms for only 5 of about 478 nouns ending in -man, and none for -woman compounds. Without a rule, pluralize(\"policeman\") gives \"policemans\", a non-word. Plural rules:\n- A known noun ending in -man takes -men, unless it is in MAN_REGULAR, a hand-reviewed list of nouns where \"man\" isn't the word man (human, shaman, talisman, ottoman, caiman, …).\n- Any word ending in -sis, at least 5 letters long, takes -ses (mitosis→mitoses).\nChecked singular rules, whose output must be a WordNet noun: -men→-man (policemen→policeman) and -ses→-sis (mitoses→mitosis). The generator's class B1 analysis uses the same plural function, so any new ambiguity is classified before tables are written." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T19:10:48.038063Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9fb15147-a447-413a-ae10-2bf324d1f882> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "P6: -man/-men and -sis/-ses rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
