<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c76d8a7f-4822-436b-9098-c3fb5594e21e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "By default, a word that no dictionary-checked step resolves (invariant, irregular/choice/WordNet form, the OTHERS rule, checked rules, known word) is returned unchanged by singularize. The free functions and `Inflector::new()` never guess. The structural acronym-plural rule (IDs→ID) stays on.\n`Inflector::builder().guess_unknown(true)` enables the guarded fallback:\n- It applies only to lower-case [a-z] words of at least 4 letters.\n- Rules: -ies→-y after a consonant; sibilant+es→strip es; -s→strip after a consonant or e.\n- A result is accepted when the whole result is a noun, or a suffix of at least 4 letters is a noun with at least 2 letters before it.\n- It refuses OTHERS words, compounds of invariants, and the listed risky endings.\nThe opt-in is documented as best-effort with a known residual, such as afterhours→afterhour. pluralize behaves identically in both modes. The NLTK differential's committed expected.tsv covers the default mode, and expected-guess.tsv records the opt-in residual." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c76d8a7f-4822-436b-9098-c3fb5594e21e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
