<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d513e420-6688-4b55-92c3-10b5cb2c4570> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "singularize order for words not handled earlier (invariant, irregular, choice, WordNet form):\n- **OTHERS step.** A word WordNet lists only as a non-noun (OTHERS: single-token non-noun lemmas ending in -s) is returned unchanged. The exception: a checked rule reduces it to a noun N and moult's own plural of N is exactly the word. Then it reduces (bats→bat because pluralize(bat)=bats). alas stays, because pluralize(ala)=alae.\n- **Checked rules, then known words.**\n- **Fallback.** It applies only to words WordNet doesn't contain in any part of speech, lower-case [a-z], at least 4 letters. Rules: -ies→-y after a consonant; sibilant+es→strip es; -s→strip after a consonant or e. A result is accepted only if the whole result is a WordNet noun, or a proper suffix of at least 4 letters is a noun with at least 2 letters before it (a plausible compound boundary). So microservices→microservice is accepted, and elap and custode are refused.\n- **Left unchanged:** compounds of an invariant noun, the listed risky endings (-as, -is, -us, -ss, -os, -ys, -ics, -ities, -wards, -selves, -ops, vowel+ses, -sses, -etes, -ales, -iformes, -ides, -facies), capitalised words, and words with digits or symbols.\nResidual risk: rare Latin and archaic entries whose ending happens to be a 4+ letter noun can still reduce to a non-word (alabastrites→alabastrite). These are listed in tools/nltk-diff/DIFFERENCES.md." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d513e420-6688-4b55-92c3-10b5cb2c4570> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
