<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e7f74f02-f48c-47fa-98b4-720ee78fc001> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/cdaaaded-bd10-485e-a590-f298e66ab80d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e7f74f02-f48c-47fa-98b4-720ee78fc001> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e7f74f02-f48c-47fa-98b4-720ee78fc001> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Plural rules for words with no irregular, choice or WordNet-form entry:\n- A known noun ending in -man takes -men unless it is in MAN_REGULAR (human, shaman, talisman, …).\n- A noun ending in -ch takes -s when it is in CH_REGULAR. This is a hand-reviewed list (39 entries) of nouns where the ch is pronounced /k/ or /x/: stomach, monarch, epoch, loch, eunuch, triptych, tech, … Other -ch nouns take -es (church, march, couch, speech).\n- Any word ending in -sis, at least 5 letters long, takes -ses.\n- Otherwise the regular plural applies.\nChecked singular rules -men→-man and -ses→-sis accept their output only when it is a WordNet noun.\nThe generator validates MAN_REGULAR and CH_REGULAR: each list is sorted, every entry is a noun with the right ending, and no entry is already settled by a form or another choice. Its class analysis uses the same plural function." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e7f74f02-f48c-47fa-98b4-720ee78fc001> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e7f74f02-f48c-47fa-98b4-720ee78fc001> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
