<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/a015bda6-ea2a-45ef-be4f-88044eade679> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/001579c2-0a0e-4a71-a2f6-984eb5b5c9da> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/195bc085-97d3-4f98-a026-c8670dad8945> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c8e818d-52b6-45c0-a39d-c111a44c6f6c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cf2837f-dd1c-44b9-a28f-20017d84c929> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Tables are generated only from the release pinned in data/MANIFEST.toml (URL + sha256); the generator refuses on a hash mismatch. Same inputs give byte-identical output (byte-sorted, no timestamps, \\n endings). Generated files are never hand-edited; bumping the release is a deliberate separate change. The 2025 Turtle releases are not usable (no inflected forms); the WN-LMF XML is the input." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:43:08.131642Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/8e547b3c-903b-4043-afbf-b23409fbde9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Pinned data, byte-identical regeneration" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4155d836-2a5e-41e2-8713-f0fd6b2730c4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4155d836-2a5e-41e2-8713-f0fd6b2730c4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Background CLI runs need closed stdin and a liveness check" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4155d836-2a5e-41e2-8713-f0fd6b2730c4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6be1f7d0-b2d8-4859-a472-15a37b2d6ee5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4155d836-2a5e-41e2-8713-f0fd6b2730c4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4155d836-2a5e-41e2-8713-f0fd6b2730c4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Run non-interactive CLIs (codex exec) in the background with `< /dev/null`, and check the output shows progress shortly after launch. In the moult 0.2.0 review, codex exec with stdin left open printed \"Reading additional input from stdin...\" and waited for hours until the user asked." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4155d836-2a5e-41e2-8713-f0fd6b2730c4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4155d836-2a5e-41e2-8713-f0fd6b2730c4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-18T03:32:29.269985Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4155d836-2a5e-41e2-8713-f0fd6b2730c4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Background CLI runs need closed stdin and a liveness check" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Measure a class before curating it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/5716d820-8bd9-4f9e-90b0-257b9c4a72f2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Before planning a hand-curated list, count how many entries fall in each class in the actual data. Let a default rule cover the bulk, and refuse or curate only the genuinely ambiguous rows (tens to low hundreds). If an ambiguous class runs into the thousands, choose a structural tie-break instead of a list. Learned when the first P1 draft proposed refusing every input where both the word and its stripped form are nouns: about 460 rows, and the class grows with WordNet's plural-form lemmas (arms, goods, customs)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:44:25.66769Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Measure a class before curating it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a844efd0-005c-4bcb-8f7a-b03d595bc463> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fc760bb9-03a7-48dd-88bb-9850b9951804> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A word list will never be complete" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/5716d820-8bd9-4f9e-90b0-257b9c4a72f2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/cdaaaded-bd10-485e-a590-f298e66ab80d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When a failure class is open-ended, such as non-words from guessing at words outside the dictionary, don't chase it by extending refusal lists or tightening heuristics after each counterexample. Choose a structural answer instead: a safe default that never guesses, plus an explicit opt-in for hosts that prefer recall. Learned from four review rounds that each found a new fallback non-word (lach, elap, perhap, afterhour). The user ended it with \"A word list will never be complete\" and chose to make the fallback opt-in." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T20:23:27.310173Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A word list will never be complete" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ac5befe4-aa57-4e64-a0ee-4030dccb3968> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c76d8a7f-4822-436b-9098-c3fb5594e21e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Generator refuses unclassified or stale policy" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/3bd26ec5-16d9-4652-8d22-6133ab4469ac> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/5716d820-8bd9-4f9e-90b0-257b9c4a72f2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "gen-data fails when any genuinely ambiguous entry (classes B, C and D) has no curated choice, when a curated entry no longer matches any ambiguity (stale), or when an invariant or supplement entry is not a WordNet noun. report prints exactly the offending entries as ready-to-paste lines, so fixing it means adding lines. Effect: a WordNet release bump cannot change behaviour on ambiguous words without a human decision." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:44:25.629918Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c3825b8b-b3a2-4238-bf18-20fb8d75ce45> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Generator refuses unclassified or stale policy" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2560de8c-6d59-4b04-b2be-fa73c7b8a205> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2560de8c-6d59-4b04-b2be-fa73c7b8a205> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2560de8c-6d59-4b04-b2be-fa73c7b8a205> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Case kept; word functions take one word, phrase functions inflect the last word" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2560de8c-6d59-4b04-b2be-fa73c7b8a205> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2560de8c-6d59-4b04-b2be-fa73c7b8a205> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "GitHub issue #2: multi-word noun phrases (labels, titles, column names) are common input, and the whitespace skip returns them unchanged with no signal, so callers find it only by test failure. Head-final English compounds (order line, dry dock) are the common case and need only the last word inflected, which keeps one-word semantics for the inflection itself. Identifier splitting and head-initial compounds stay out of scope." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2560de8c-6d59-4b04-b2be-fa73c7b8a205> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2560de8c-6d59-4b04-b2be-fa73c7b8a205> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-18T00:56:20.263484Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2560de8c-6d59-4b04-b2be-fa73c7b8a205> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Case kept; word functions take one word, phrase functions inflect the last word" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/371441b9-4640-4cef-8b7e-63f9c17e6f3c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/371441b9-4640-4cef-8b7e-63f9c17e6f3c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "code-diverged" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/371441b9-4640-4cef-8b7e-63f9c17e6f3c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: P3: Conservative fallback, compound-boundary head check, OTHERS-aware" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/371441b9-4640-4cef-8b7e-63f9c17e6f3c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/371441b9-4640-4cef-8b7e-63f9c17e6f3c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Codex round 2 found two problems. The 3-letter head check still accepted elaps→elap via the noun \"lap\". And checked rules ran before the OTHERS lookup, so alas became ala. Moving OTHERS first froze 16 genuine noun plurals that WordNet also lists as adjectives or verbs (bats, nuts, tops, needs). The final rule reduces an OTHERS word only when the reduction round-trips through moult's own plural, which keeps the generated data pure." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/371441b9-4640-4cef-8b7e-63f9c17e6f3c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/371441b9-4640-4cef-8b7e-63f9c17e6f3c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T20:09:01.356029Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/371441b9-4640-4cef-8b7e-63f9c17e6f3c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: P3: Conservative fallback, compound-boundary head check, OTHERS-aware" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: P4: -oes/-ves plurals only where WordNet lists them (no mechanical filter)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The step 1 gate measured the mechanical filter's drops. It treated quiz/quizzes and fez/fezzes as doubling variants alongside bus/busses and gas/gasses, so pluralize(\"quiz\") would give \"quizes\", contradicting the acceptance table. Whether a doubled form is the standard plural is a judgement call that no rule can make. So the generator applies no filter. The few such lemmas are classified by hand in class D, which keeps the generated tables pure WordNet extraction." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:57:41.305336Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/78d202f9-b1fb-4435-9870-8a5a1f89dde2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: P4: -oes/-ves plurals only where WordNet lists them (no mechanical filter)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bad2ffd-e0fc-49f1-b842-a7e2c2b66e2b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bad2ffd-e0fc-49f1-b842-a7e2c2b66e2b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bad2ffd-e0fc-49f1-b842-a7e2c2b66e2b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: P3: Unknown-word fallback is opt-in (guess_unknown)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bad2ffd-e0fc-49f1-b842-a7e2c2b66e2b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bad2ffd-e0fc-49f1-b842-a7e2c2b66e2b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Every codex review round (1 to 4) found another non-word from the unchecked fallback: lach, aby, elap, perhap, afterhour, belowstair. Each fix extended a list or tightened a heuristic. The user decided that guessing should be off by default, observing that a word list will never be complete. The failure class is open-ended, so the structural answer is a safe default with an explicit opt-in, not more lists." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bad2ffd-e0fc-49f1-b842-a7e2c2b66e2b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bad2ffd-e0fc-49f1-b842-a7e2c2b66e2b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T20:23:27.082892Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bad2ffd-e0fc-49f1-b842-a7e2c2b66e2b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: P3: Unknown-word fallback is opt-in (guess_unknown)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/97dcde84-dd7b-4ae2-a8ba-ce1f89082f71> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/97dcde84-dd7b-4ae2-a8ba-ce1f89082f71> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "code-diverged" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/97dcde84-dd7b-4ae2-a8ba-ce1f89082f71> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: D8: Case restoration by origin-aware per-character copy" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/97dcde84-dd7b-4ae2-a8ba-ce1f89082f71> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/97dcde84-dd7b-4ae2-a8ba-ce1f89082f71> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Codex review rounds 1 and 2 found two cases. Lowercasings that change length lost case (İstanbul), and all-caps irregular plurals got lower-case endings (CHILD→CHILDren). Inferring the case from the shape of the result can't tell an acronym suffix from an irregular ending, so the resolver now passes the origin of the change explicitly." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/97dcde84-dd7b-4ae2-a8ba-ce1f89082f71> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/97dcde84-dd7b-4ae2-a8ba-ce1f89082f71> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T20:09:01.491823Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/97dcde84-dd7b-4ae2-a8ba-ce1f89082f71> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: D8: Case restoration by origin-aware per-character copy" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9ff2191b-ca12-4da1-b4ea-b67a9508c88f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9ff2191b-ca12-4da1-b4ea-b67a9508c88f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "code-diverged" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9ff2191b-ca12-4da1-b4ea-b67a9508c88f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: P3: Conservative fallback with known-head check" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9ff2191b-ca12-4da1-b4ea-b67a9508c88f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9ff2191b-ca12-4da1-b4ea-b67a9508c88f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Codex review round 1 flagged a showstopper: the unchecked fallback still invented non-words (laches→lach, abies→aby). A known-head check fixes it by accepting a reduction only when the result ends in a WordNet noun. That cut fallback disagreements with NLTK by 634 rows, and every modern-jargon control still reduces. The check then exposed perhaps→perhap: P3 says the fallback fires only for words WordNet doesn't contain, but the code consulted nouns only. WordNet's single-token non-noun lemmas ending in -s (1,448 words, about 15 KB) are now a generated known-word table, so the fallback never fires on them." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9ff2191b-ca12-4da1-b4ea-b67a9508c88f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9ff2191b-ca12-4da1-b4ea-b67a9508c88f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T19:52:04.686451Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/9ff2191b-ca12-4da1-b4ea-b67a9508c88f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: P3: Conservative fallback with known-head check" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/aa62790f-597f-4e47-bfc8-b07b48f6d599> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/aa62790f-597f-4e47-bfc8-b07b48f6d599> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/aa62790f-597f-4e47-bfc8-b07b48f6d599> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: P3: Conservative fallback for unknown words (tightened)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/aa62790f-597f-4e47-bfc8-b07b48f6d599> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/aa62790f-597f-4e47-bfc8-b07b48f6d599> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The NLTK differential ran over 287,755 words, including /usr/share/dict/words. It showed the original P3 rules producing non-words on unknown words: backwards→backward, themselves→themselve, superspecies→superspecy, moses→mos, tholos→tholo, agaricales→agaricale, kubernetes→kubernete. That violates the invariant that leaving a word unchanged beats inventing a non-word. The tightened version keeps the rules useful for modern jargon (microservices, endpoints, workflows) and refuses the endings and compounds the differential showed to be risky. The user's choice of a conservative strip over leaving every unknown word unchanged still stands." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/aa62790f-597f-4e47-bfc8-b07b48f6d599> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/aa62790f-597f-4e47-bfc8-b07b48f6d599> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T19:26:41.33665Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/aa62790f-597f-4e47-bfc8-b07b48f6d599> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: P3: Conservative fallback for unknown words (tightened)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b163a5db-3e5e-4237-98f3-d754b3bc6c7b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b163a5db-3e5e-4237-98f3-d754b3bc6c7b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b163a5db-3e5e-4237-98f3-d754b3bc6c7b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Head-initial compounds inflect the wrong word; documented as the caller's job" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b163a5db-3e5e-4237-98f3-d754b3bc6c7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b163a5db-3e5e-4237-98f3-d754b3bc6c7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The original consequence text contained a garbled example (passer by); restated cleanly." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b163a5db-3e5e-4237-98f3-d754b3bc6c7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b163a5db-3e5e-4237-98f3-d754b3bc6c7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-18T00:56:37.180235Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b163a5db-3e5e-4237-98f3-d754b3bc6c7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Head-initial compounds inflect the wrong word; documented as the caller's job" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: P6: -man/-men, -sis/-ses and /k/ -ch rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Codex review round 3 found that the -ch plural rule always added -es, so pluralize(\"stomach\") gave \"stomaches\", and the same for loch and monarch. No WordNet form covers them, and the round-trip test can't catch it because singularize strips the -es back. The fix follows the existing MAN_REGULAR pattern: a hand-reviewed, generator-validated exception list." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T20:16:32.492702Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d3e94a2c-dec6-4ba1-9290-efe4796b6477> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: P6: -man/-men, -sis/-ses and /k/ -ch rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Verification gates for 0.1" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/3bd26ec5-16d9-4652-8d22-6133ab4469ac> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/64a11323-9da6-405a-a37e-4f3eb843e98a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6be1f7d0-b2d8-4859-a472-15a37b2d6ee5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9b292ee7-ec7b-4131-a33a-300725e9dca5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Done only when: tests/cases.rs un-ignored and passing; NLTK WordNetLemmatizer differential run with every intentional difference listed (expected.tsv reproducible); gen-data --check byte-identical (CI job + fixture determinism test); cargo fmt --check, clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings, test --workspace clean; cargo package --list exactly the intended files and .crate well under 10 MB; binary-size and compile-time cost measured and recorded in README." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:43:08.073865Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/58238d19-563a-4127-bc1e-3f7bbd063886> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Verification gates for 0.1" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/5e2a22ed-b331-4ccd-9974-07868d0d3e0d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/5e2a22ed-b331-4ccd-9974-07868d0d3e0d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Static allocation-free tables" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/5e2a22ed-b331-4ccd-9974-07868d0d3e0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/30e45192-cd0e-479f-ba52-0b7aad475394> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/5e2a22ed-b331-4ccd-9974-07868d0d3e0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/5e2a22ed-b331-4ccd-9974-07868d0d3e0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Tables are static, sorted and binary-searched; nothing parsed at startup, nothing lazily built. Source size and compiled-binary cost of the noun index must be measured and kept reasonable (target ≤0.6 MB binary cost, ≤2 s clean build)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/5e2a22ed-b331-4ccd-9974-07868d0d3e0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/5e2a22ed-b331-4ccd-9974-07868d0d3e0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:43:08.020257Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/5e2a22ed-b331-4ccd-9974-07868d0d3e0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Static allocation-free tables" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hot-path API safe to show users" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/20157892-bc76-4766-9c99-df01009eb71b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/b9851667-ab87-40ac-bffd-99cd5802ffd2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Every result deterministic and safe to display: never a non-word where a rule over-fires (unchanged is the safe failure); cheap calls (avoid allocation when the word comes back unchanged); optional caller-supplied override layer for domain forms (SKUs, ETAs, personnel) checked before built-in data, with no global mutable state; plain free functions remain the zero-config path." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-17T18:43:08.046236Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/a3e3108a-6c7f-46ea-b998-7c938688f5a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Hot-path API safe to show users" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
